-- title:
--   Triple-overlap identity for the chart automorphisms of a cocycle
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a commutative local artinian ring $B$ with algebraically closed residue field, and a commutative $B$-algebra $B_1$ whose structure map is surjective, has nilpotent kernel $I=\ker(B\to B_1)$ contained in the maximal ideal, and satisfies the smallness condition $I\cdot\mathfrak m_B=0$; assume $q$ is nilpotent in $B$. Over $B_1$ one is given $f_1:A_1\to\operatorname{Spec}B_1$ with a commutative relative group law $L_1$ (so $L_1$ assigns functorially to each base $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}B_1$ a group structure on the $T$-points of $f_1$), satisfying the bundle of properties smooth, proper, connected fibres and existence of a group law; a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $B$ together with formal coordinates $\theta_1$ for $L_1$ with respect to $F\otimes_BB_1$; the hypothesis that every point of $f_1$ over a $B_1$-algebra $C$ killed by $q^m$ is infinitesimal along some nilpotent ideal of $C$; and the height condition that for every surjective ring map $\rho:B\to k$ onto a field the quotient of $k[[X_1,X_2]]$ by the ideal generated by the $q$-th iterated multiplication series of $F\otimes_\rho k$ has $k$-dimension $q^4$. Further data: a finitely generated $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B$-module $V$ with compatible $B$-action and central opposite action, and an injective $B$-linear $\iota:V\to B$ whose image is $I$; a bare deformation $D_0$ of $(f_1,L_1)$ over $B$, that is a scheme $D_0.A$ with separated $D_0.f:D_0.A\to\operatorname{Spec}B$, a commutative relative group law $D_0.L$, the same bundle of geometric properties, and a map $D_0.g:A_1\to D_0.A$ making the square over $B\to B_1$ cartesian; a finite ordered affine open cover $\mathcal U$ of $D_0.A$, an index $i_0$, sections $e_0$ over $B$ and $e_1$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B$ of the chart $U_{i_0}$ (respectively of its base change) through which the identity section of the group law factors; for each $1$-simplex $s$ (a strictly increasing pair of indices, with $U_s$ the corresponding intersection) a ring isomorphism $\sigma_s:\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B\otimes_B\Gamma(D_0.A,U_s)\to\Gamma$ of the base-changed intersection, normalised on $1\otimes x$ and on $a\otimes1$ as the canonical pullback and structure maps; a point derivation $c$ at $e_1$ on the sections of the base-changed chart $U_{i_0}$, with values in the $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B$-linear maps from $V^\ast$ to the $1$-cochains of the unit $\mathcal O$-module presheaf of the base-changed cover, all of whose values are killed by the Čech differential $d^1$ (the cocycle condition); and for each $1$-simplex $s$ a self-isomorphism $\tau_s$ of $U_s$ which is compatible with $D_0.f$, satisfies $(D_0.g|_{U_s})$ followed by $\tau_s$ equals $D_0.g|_{U_s}$, and whose tangent coordinates realise $c$: there are maps $c_s$ for which the predicate [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.IsTangentCoordsOfPairAt`](def/AlgebraicGeometry_TangentCoordsOfPairAt.html#L31) holds for the ideal $I$, the pair $(\iota,V)$, the ring $\Gamma(D_0.A,U_s)$, the two maps given by the canonical affine presentation of $U_s$ and by $\tau_s$ followed by the inclusion, the base-changed group law over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B$, and the chart $U_{i_0}$ — namely, there is a point of the thickening $(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B\otimes_B\Gamma(D_0.A,U_s))\otimes\mathrm{TrivSqZeroExt}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,B,V)$ in the reduced total space lying over the square-zero base, which is a tangent vector of the given pair, whose group-law translate factors through $U_{i_0}$, and from which $c_s$ is the extracted tangent coordinate function — and $\sigma_s\circ c_s$ agrees with the $s$-component of $c$. The conclusion: for every $2$-simplex $r$ (a strictly increasing triple of indices) there are three endomorphisms $\rho_0,\rho_1,\rho_2$ of the triple intersection $U_r$ such that for each $j$, $\rho_j$ followed by the inclusion $U_r\subseteq U_{\partial_jr}$ equals that inclusion followed by $\tau_{\partial_jr}$, and $\rho_1=\rho_2$ followed by $\rho_0$.
--
--   This is the cocycle step in re-gluing a deformation from Čech data: the chart automorphisms $\tau_s$ attached to a $1$-cocycle of infinitesimal automorphisms restrict to each triple overlap, and there the restriction over the outer pair is the composite of the restrictions over the two adjacent pairs. It is used by [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isRegluingBy_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.exists_isRegluingBy_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt), which assembles the $\tau_s$ into a new deformation.
